_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 11
---
order: 11
---
short_label: VI.11
---
statement: To find a third proportional to two given straight lines.
---
red_highlight: yes
---
proof:

Let *AB* and *AC* be the two given straight lines, and let them be placed so as to contain any angle.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="250" height="220" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="VI.11 diagram" src="propVI11.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "VI.11",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;80,30",
            "B;point;free;60,90",
            "C;point;free;135,100",
            "D;point;extend;A,B,A,C",
            "E;point;similar;A,D,A,B,C",
            "ADE;polygon;triangle;A,D,E;0;0;black;random",
            "ABC;polygon;triangle;A,B,C;0;0;black;random"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

It is required to find a third proportional to *AB* and *AC.*

Produce them to the points *D* and *E,* and make *BD* equal to *AC.* Join *BC,* and draw *DE* through *D* parallel to it. [!just I.3; I.31]

Then since *BC* is parallel to a side *DE* of the triangle *ADE,* therefore, proportionally, *AB* is to *BD* as *AC* is to *CE.* [!just VI.2]

But *BD* equals *AC,* therefore *AB* is to *AC* as *AC* is to *CE.* [!just V.7]

Therefore a third proportional *CE* has been found to two given straight lines *AB* and *AC.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.F.</div>
<br clear="all">
---
body:

If *a* and *b* are two magnitudes, then their third proportional is a magnitude *c* such that *a* : *b* = *b* : *c.* The third proportional is needed whenever a duplicate ratio is needed when the ratio itself is known. The duplicate ratio for *a* : *b* is *a* : *c.*

#### Use of this proposition

This construction is used in propositions @VI.19, @VI.22, and a few propositions in Book X.
